meta {
  name: BluPrint API
}

docs {
  # BluPrint API

  A collection for testing the API by hand. The automated tests prove the
  contract (`apps/api/src/**/*.int-spec.ts`); this exists for the other case —
  opening a route, looking at the response body, and debugging real cookies and
  headers.

  ## Before running

  1. `docker compose up -d --wait` — Postgres, once per session.
  2. `.env` with `BETTER_AUTH_SECRET` and `ALLOW_SELF_SIGNUP=true`. Without the
     second, step 4 answers 403 and the collection looks broken — self-signup is
     scaffolding and defaults to off
     (see `docs/adr/0011-self-signup-is-scaffolding.md`).
  3. `bun run dev` — starts the API on `:3000` and the web app on `:5173`.
  4. Select the **local** environment in the top right corner. Without it
     `{{baseUrl}}` does not resolve and Bruno answers `Invalid URL`.

  The environment defines two variables: `baseUrl` (`http://localhost:3000`) and
  `webOrigin` (`http://localhost:5173`, the web app's origin).

  ## Suggested order

  | Seq | Request | Checks |
  | --- | --- | --- |
  | 1–2 | Health check | The API is up and the database answers |
  | 3 | Unknown route | The `{"error": "..."}` error contract still holds |
  | 4 | Sign up | Creates account, session, organization, `admin` membership and three licenses |
  | 5 | Sign in | Signs back in with the account from step 4 |
  | 6 | Current session | Confirms the cookie is valid |
  | 7 | My projects | Lists visible projects, with the caller's role in each |

  ## Two things that confuse

  **The cookie is stored automatically.** Sign-up and sign-in return
  `better-auth.session_token` in `Set-Cookie`, and Bruno reuses it on the next
  calls. To test as an anonymous visitor, clear Bruno's cookies first.

  **Every auth request sends `Origin: {{webOrigin}}`.** Bruno sends
  `Origin: null` when nobody sets the header, and Better Auth rejects `null`
  with 403 `MISSING_OR_NULL_ORIGIN` — it is what a sandboxed iframe sends. The
  check only runs on requests **with a cookie**, so without the header the first
  call passes and every later one fails, which looks random and is not.

  ## What is not here

  Better Auth generates dozens of routes. Only the three on the happy path are
  documented — sign-up, sign-in and session — which is what you want at hand on
  the first cookie error. Documenting the rest would be maintenance with no
  reader.
}
